{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinInfoLowerBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinInfoLowerBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinHorizonLowerBound","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Log"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.treeSearch_info","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.treeSearch_info","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinInfoLowerBound.lean#L79-L84","doc":"The depth-`d` ternary search carries exactly `d` trits: its normal form\n`3^d` has `log₃ = d`, the filtration level. So `treeSearch d`'s sequential\ncost `3^d` (`treeSearch_hcost`) and its information depth `d` are the two\nends of the query spectrum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.horizon_depth_ge_info","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.horizon_depth_ge_info","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinInfoLowerBound.lean#L70-L77","doc":"**The horizon's decision-depth floor.** Any ternary decision process whose\nreachable leaves cover the horizon (`numLeaves ≤ 3^d`) has depth\n`≥ info(H) = c`. The information-theoretic complement of the sequential-walk\nstep bound `treeSearch_hcost`: the *optimal-query* floor is `c` trits, while\nthe *sequential-walk* cost is `3^c` leaf visits. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.info_depth_lower_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.info_depth_lower_bound","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinInfoLowerBound.lean#L60-L68","doc":"**Entropy floor — the rigorous `info(n)` lower bound.** A ternary\ndecision/branching process that must distinguish `N` outcomes at depth `d`\n— i.e. whose `3^d` reachable leaves cover them (`N ≤ 3^d`) — needs depth at\nleast `log₃ N`. Each step reveals at most one trit, so `d` steps separate at\nmost `3^d` outcomes. Pure counting; unconditional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.numLeaves_eq_three_pow_info","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.numLeaves_eq_three_pow_info","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinInfoLowerBound.lean#L54-L58","doc":"`numLeaves = 3^{info}` — the information count is exact, not merely a bound:\nthe horizon has precisely `3^{info(H)}` leaves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.horizonInfo_eq_filtrationLevel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.horizonInfo_eq_filtrationLevel","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinInfoLowerBound.lean#L48-L52","doc":"`info(H) = c` — the trit-information equals the filtration level, exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.horizonInfo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.horizonInfo","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinInfoLowerBound.lean#L42-L46","doc":"**Information content of the computational horizon, in trits** — the base-3\nlogarithm of the leaf count. Since the ternary resolution tree has\n`numLeaves = 3^c`, this is exactly the crossing count `c`: the number of\nindependent ternary resolutions the observer must fix. ","signatureChunk":0}]}